Main transactional document for requesting and ordering goods/services from suppliers (RFQ → Purchase Order), managing the full procurement lifecycle.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Create RFQs and convert to Purchase Orders
Manage multi-line purchases with prices, taxes, and delivery dates
Handle approvals, vendor confirmations, and order updates
Generate incoming shipments (stock.picking)
Vendor bills matching (3-way matching)
Purchase agreements / blanket orders / call for tenders
Reporting: purchase analysis, spend by supplier, on-time delivery

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread + activity.mixin)
Key Fields:
name (sequenced: POxxxx / RFxxxx), state (draft/sent/to_approve/purchase/done/cancel)
partner_id → res.partner (supplier, required)
date_order, date_planned, requisition_id
amount_untaxed, amount_tax, amount_total
One2many: order_line → purchase.order.line
picking_ids, invoice_ids (Many2many)
fiscal_position_id, payment_term_id, incoterm_id

Critical Hooks: button_confirm, button_approve, action_create_invoice, _create_picking, onchange_partner_id
Security: purchase.group_purchase_manager + company + own documents rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
purchase order, PO, RFQ, request for quotation, vendor order, supplier order, procurement order, purchase requisition, blanket order, purchase agreement, vendor purchase, purchase confirmation, draft RFQ, sent RFQ, confirmed purchase order, pending purchase, awaiting receipt, to receive, cancelled purchase order, purchase status, purchase order state
Related Models (most joined):

purchase.order.line (child lines — most important)
res.partner (supplier)
product.product / product.template
stock.picking (receipts)
account.move (vendor bills)
purchase.requisition
stock.warehouse

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
purchase.order is Odoo’s core procurement model representing RFQs and Purchase Orders with supplier, order lines, totals, state, and planned dates. It drives supplier confirmation, incoming stock moves, vendor bill creation, 3-way matching, and full integration between Purchase, Inventory, and Accounting modules.